# Hand-written fixture for cube.obj.
newmtl GroundSurface
Kd 0.3 0.3 0.3

# brick's `d` and `Ns` are single fractional digits chosen (not 0.9/250) because those
# happen to parse identically under tinyobjloader's not-correctly-rounded number parser
# and strtod -- these do not, so obj_sidecars.test can actually tell the two apart.
newmtl brick
Kd 0.7 0.3 0.2
Ks 0.1 0.1 0.1
d 0.7
Ns 0.7
map_Kd brick.png
# illum and map_Ks are typed MTL directives tinyobjloader parses into fields of its
# own; they are here to pin that every unmapped directive still reaches `other`.
illum 2
map_Ks spec.png

# `Tr 0.3` (not `d`) so transparency is taken from Tr directly: a 1 - (1 - Tr) round
# trip would print 0.30000000000000004 instead.
newmtl RoofSurface
Kd 0.9 0.06 0.09
Tr 0.3
